<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yuhi V Musinga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1883–<a href="/years/1944">1944</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Musinga</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yuhi V Musinga was king of Rwanda from 1896 to 1931. Brought to the throne as a youth by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coup-of-rucunshu">Coup of Rucunshu</a>, he ruled at first under the control of his mother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanjogera">Kanjogera</a> and her kinsmen, and in 1897 accepted German protection. He made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nyanza-rwanda">Nyanza</a> the permanent royal seat. Under Belgian rule he resisted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> and colonial reforms, and in 1931 the Belgians deposed and exiled him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yuhi-v-musinga.jpg" alt="Yuhi V Musinga" width="320" height="446" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown photographer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:YuhiVMusinga.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
